{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792601633,"nonce":"qqXTavcLEotJHiE76sbRVD/Slb0=","title":"Reuse typed workspace dependencies between LSP pages","message":"Each document currently creates a fresh CompilationUnit, loads the standard library and initialization macros, and rediscovers and types the import closure. The declaration index does not retain typed dependency state. Opening or reopening pages repeats this work, while keeping independent per-page compiler graphs grows memory.\n\nReproducer: run the native language server in the sibling RayDE workspace with installed Haxe stdlib discovery and open Welcome, ImagePreview, ExplorerOutline, CommandCenter and LspClient in sequence, then close and reopen Welcome. The pre-change probe took 15.270s, 10.397s, 13.548s, 16.541s, 3.272s and 19.780s respectively during concurrent validation builds. These are observational timings, not an isolated benchmark.\n\nShare compiler-local identities within a compatible typed graph, avoid rediscovering already typed import closures, validate source/configuration generations including unsaved overlays, and bound resident graphs. Eviction must release state and reanalysis must use the latest buffers. Do not replace an installed Haxe library with a bundled Rayzor BLADE manifest.","files":null}]}